      "attributes": [
        {
          "doc_text": " Compute w * 10^q using an extended-precision float representation.",
          "path": "doc",
          "range": [
            244,
            314
          ],
          "style": "outer"
        },
        {
          "doc_text": "",
          "path": "doc",
          "range": [
            315,
            318
          ],
          "style": "outer"
        },
        {
          "doc_text": " Fast conversion of a the significant digits and decimal exponent",
          "path": "doc",
          "range": [
            319,
            387
          ],
          "style": "outer"
        },
        {
          "doc_text": " a float to an extended representation with a binary float. This",
          "path": "doc",
          "range": [
            388,
            455
          ],
          "style": "outer"
        },
        {
          "doc_text": " algorithm will accurately parse the vast majority of cases,",
          "path": "doc",
          "range": [
            456,
            519
          ],
          "style": "outer"
        },
        {
          "doc_text": " and uses a 128-bit representation (with a fallback 192-bit",
          "path": "doc",
          "range": [
            520,
            582
          ],
          "style": "outer"
        },
        {
          "doc_text": " representation).",
          "path": "doc",
          "range": [
            583,
            603
          ],
          "style": "outer"
        },
        {
          "doc_text": "",
          "path": "doc",
          "range": [
            604,
            607
          ],
          "style": "outer"
        },
        {
          "doc_text": " This algorithm scales the exponent by the decimal exponent",
          "path": "doc",
          "range": [
            608,
            670
          ],
          "style": "outer"
        },
        {
          "doc_text": " using pre-computed powers-of-5, and calculates if the",
          "path": "doc",
          "range": [
            671,
            728
          ],
          "style": "outer"
        },
        {
          "doc_text": " representation can be unambiguously rounded to the nearest",
          "path": "doc",
          "range": [
            729,
            791
          ],
          "style": "outer"
        },
        {
          "doc_text": " machine float. Near-halfway cases are not handled here,",
          "path": "doc",
          "range": [
            792,
            851
          ],
          "style": "outer"
        },
        {
          "doc_text": " and are represented by a negative, biased binary exponent.",
          "path": "doc",
          "range": [
            852,
            914
          ],
          "style": "outer"
        },
        {
          "doc_text": "",
          "path": "doc",
          "range": [
            915,
            918
          ],
          "style": "outer"
        },
        {
          "doc_text": " The algorithm is described in detail in \"Daniel Lemire, Number Parsing",
          "path": "doc",
          "range": [
            919,
            993
          ],
          "style": "outer"
        },
        {
          "doc_text": " at a Gigabyte per Second\" in section 5, \"Fast Algorithm\", and",
          "path": "doc",
          "range": [
            994,
            1059
          ],
          "style": "outer"
        },
        {
          "doc_text": " section 6, \"Exact Numbers And Ties\", available online:",
          "path": "doc",
          "range": [
            1060,
            1118
          ],
          "style": "outer"
        },
        {
          "doc_text": " <https://arxiv.org/abs/2101.11408.pdf>.",
          "path": "doc",
          "range": [
            1119,
            1162
          ],
          "style": "outer"
        }
      ],
      "body_range": [
        1229,
        5019
      ],
